&lt;li&gt;Create compelling AI behaviours &amp;amp; attack patterns that provide an exciting experience and appropriately challenging for players&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse combat data, player feedback, and internal playtests to refine and iterate on enemy and boss designs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work concurrently on multiple features at varying stages of development, managing priorities effectively as content pipelines run in parallel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document and communicate enemy and boss design concepts clearly to ensure alignment across all development teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in Combat / Enemy Design or an equivalent role in the video game industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least one shipped title in a design role for a Shooter / Action / RPG title&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and implementing enemy AI, behaviours, and encounters for action games&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on a first-person or third-person game&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the Unreal game engine&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to analyse gameplay data and player feedback to inform and balance design decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong visual &amp;amp; verbal communication skills with the ability to work effectively across cross-disciplinary teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to manage multiple designs in a fast-paced development environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about action games with a deep understanding of what makes enemy designs engaging and memorable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
